{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791563179,"nonce":"o+Fvl18KhchzVKdBuyaXmRsX+7k=","title":"Accessibility: a platform accessibility tree from the scene","message":"Neither blinc_ts nor ashui exposes anything to screen readers. A GUI SDK others build frameworks on has to: roles, names, states and actions per node, focus and live regions, published to the platform's accessibility API (for example through AccessKit, which winit integrates), from the same tree layout and hit-testing use. Built-in elements get their roles by default; the host interface sets role and aria-style attributes. After the host interface and events land.","files":null}]}